.TH IMPROV-SET 1 "" "improv" "Improv Manual"
.SH NAME
improv\-set \- Set an input cell
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBimprov set\fR [OPTIONS] <db> <measure\-id> <value>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Set an input cell.
.PP
The value is parsed by the measure\*(Aqs type: a number, true or false, or verbatim text. \-\-at maps category names to item names; omit it for a scalar cell. Pairs may be comma\-joined (\-\-at Time=Q1,Product=A), space\-separated (\-\-at Time=Q1 Product=A) or in repeated flags; they are merged, and a category may appear only once.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-at\fR \fI<Cat=Item>...\fR
The cell\*(Aqs coordinate: Category=Item pairs, comma\-joined, space\-separated, or in repeated \-\-at flags
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIdb\fR>
The model store: a file, or postgres://USER@HOST/DB?model=NAME
.TP
<\fImeasure\-id\fR>
A measure\*(Aqs numeric id
.TP
<\fIvalue\fR>
The cell\*(Aqs value
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR improv (1).
